// Writes conformance/server.v1.json: HTTP scenarios generated by running the TypeScript handler (the reference) over
// a service. Each scenario has an initial document, handler options and ordered steps; a step is one request with the
// clock (editor and options.now), the status, every response header and the body (parsed JSON, or text).
//   routes      every route with good and bad requests (HEAD, OPTIONS, 404/405/413/415, query errors, undo/redo ...)
//   options-*   readOnly, a fixed actor, basePath, CORS, a small body limit
//   walk-N      seeded random sequences of actions through POST /actions/{name}, steered by the live document
//   inputs      every action fed mutated inputs, so the schema checker's messages are pinned too
// Go and Python must reproduce every response. The generator never calls the handler with a random transaction id.
import { writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';
